{
  "_id": "6ac20220773a0037682c073a",
  "Package": "spicyR",
  "Type": "Package",
  "Title": "Test Changes in the Co-Localisation of Cell Types Between Groups\nof Patients",
  "Version": "1.99.6",
  "Authors@R": "c(\nperson(\"Nicolas\", \"Canete\", , \"nicolas.canete@sydney.edu.au\", role = \"aut\"),\nperson(\"Ellis\", \"Patrick\", , \"ellis.patrick@sydney.edu.au\", role = c(\"aut\", \"cre\")),\nperson(\"Sadiq\", \"Dohadwalla\", role = \"aut\"),\nperson(\"Elijah\", \"Willie\", , \"ewillie0004@gmail.com\", role = \"aut\"),\nperson(\"Nicholas\", \"Robertson\", , \"nicholas.robertson@sydney.edu.au\", role = \"ctb\"),\nperson(\"Alex\", \"Qin\", , \"alex.qin@sydney.edu.au\", role = \"ctb\"),\nperson(\"Farhan\", \"Ameen\", ,\"farhan.ameen@sydney.edu.au\", role = \"ctb\"),\nperson(\"Shreya\", \"Rao\", ,\"shreya.rajeshrao@sydney.edu.au\", role = \"ctb\")\n)",
  "Description": "spicyR tests whether the spatial co-localisation of pairs\nof cell types differs between groups of patients, or is\nassociated with patient outcome, in cell-resolution spatial\nomics data (imaging mass cytometry, CODEX, MIBI, Xenium, CosMx\nand others). Its default method, spicyR Cell, counts the cells\nof one type within a radius of each cell of another and\ncompares the count with its exact expectation under random\nlabelling of the observed cells. Images are combined within\npatients by a frailty generalised estimating equation, and\ndifferences are tested with a small-sample cluster-robust (CR2)\nvariance with patients as the units. Covariates, several\nconditions, several radii and survival outcomes are supported,\nand the original image-level test is kept as an option. The\ncomputations run in a C++ core shared with the Python package\nspicyr.",
  "License": "GPL (>=2)",
